    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0087" n="17" xml:id="pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Commercial Agreement/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-21T17:00:00+01:00">September 21, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 21—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. Consulate’s No. 256, September 21, noon, paragraph 6. Request confirmation
                    United States signature Pan American Agreement in time for use by Belgian
                    representative who contemplates reopening question in Second Committee tomorrow
                    morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
